---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Add objects of one kind to a board; the kind word is the default kind of every --items item.
Without --at each goes to a free corner, in --frame if given, else in the frame a linked object sits in. It prints one line per object with @N and its link.
An image or a file is uploaded first; a link card takes its title from the page. With --items, #N names an earlier item as an arrow end, and one write holds all of them.

USAGE
  holst object add code <board> [<text>] [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board: id, link or part of its name
  text    The text; lines become paragraphs; the title of a frame or task; the code of a code block; the name of an icon, e.g. rocket-launch

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws    Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --frame frame     Put it inside this frame: id, link, title or part of a title; --at counts from its corner
      --at x,y          The top-left corner in board units, from the frame's corner with --frame; a free corner by default
      --language name   A code block's language for its highlighting; none marked by default
      --theme theme     A code block's theme: light or dark; light by default
      --items file      Many in one write: a JSON array or JSON lines file, - for stdin; its keys are the flags of one call
  -n, --dry-run         Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o add code "Roadmap" "$(cat main.rs)" --language rust --theme dark

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
